# The Raspberry Pi 4 Model B: its 40-pin header J8 and the pins its firmware and board keep for themselves.
board rpi4b
name "Raspberry Pi 4 Model B"
soc bcm2711
source "Raspberry Pi 4 Model B Reduced Schematics", Raspberry Pi Ltd, RP-008345-DS-1, connector J8
header J8 40
# position  pin   (the other positions are power and ground)
3   2
5   3
7   4
8   14
10  15
11  17
12  18
13  27
15  22
16  23
18  24
19  10
21  9
22  25
23  11
24  8
26  7
27  0
28  1
29  5
31  6
32  12
33  13
35  19
36  16
37  26
38  20
40  21
reserved 0-1 the HAT ID EEPROM (ID_SD, ID_SC: "do not use these pins for anything other than attaching an I2C ID EEPROM")
reserved 14-15 the firmware's serial console (TXD0, RXD0)
reserved 28-57 not on the header: used on the board
